 "description": "Records a non-SAFE agreement (option, RSU, RSA, FAST advisor agreement, board consent) against a company. Without signed_at it creates a draft and touches nothing else. SIGNED_AT IS NOT A DATE FIELD \u2014 it is a declaration that the document is already executed, and for a FAST it WRITES TO THE CAP TABLE: it puts the advisor on the register as a stakeholder and issues them an option holding carrying the equity percentage and the FAST's fixed 24-month / 3-month-cliff vesting. Set it ONLY when the person tells you the agreement has been signed, and say what it will do before you do it. An unsigned FAST grants nothing, so leaving signed_at empty is always the safe choice. PARTY: the advisor is matched to an existing stakeholder by EXACT name and created fresh otherwise, so a spelling that differs from the register adds a SECOND row for the same person \u2014 the twin holds no equity, so ownership views hide it while stakeholder counts include it. Call GetListCapTableStakeholders first and pass stakeholder_id whenever the advisor is already on the register. advisor_equity_pct is a percentage like \"0.50\" (a trailing % is accepted); effective_date is YYYY-MM-DD and is the date vesting runs from.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "properties": {
   "companyId": {
    "description": "UUID value wrapper.",
    "properties": {
     "value": {
      "format": "uuid",
      "type": "string"
     }
    },
    "type": "object"
   },
   "fastTerms": {
    "properties": {
     "advisorName": {
      "description": "Human-readable name (1-255 Unicode chars).",
      "properties": {
       "value": {
        "maxLength": 255,
        "minLength": 1,
        "type": "string"
       }
      },
      "type": "object"
     },
     "advisorTitle": {
      "maxLength": 200,
      "type": "string"
     },
     "companyName": {
      "description": "Human-readable name (1-255 Unicode chars).",
      "properties": {
       "value": {
        "maxLength": 255,
        "minLength": 1,
        "type": "string"
       }
      },
      "type": "object"
     },
     "effectiveDate": {
